  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "### Fixed\n\n- [A repeated `--script` flag no longer silently drops all but the last occurrence](https://github.com/ionide/FSharp.Analyzers.SDK/issues/336). Every list-valued flag now accumulates the way `--project` and `--analyzers-path` already did, so `--script a.fsx --script b.fsx` means the same as `--script a.fsx b.fsx`. Previously a caller that built its arguments in a loop analyzed a subset of what it asked for and still got a clean run reported. The `--treat-as-*`, `--exclude-files`, `--include-files`, `--exclude-analyzers` and `--include-analyzers` flags rejected a repeat outright and now accumulate too.",
